MENTOR: We'll work on Title. Here's the comp at 1 s, in the middle of its first move.

From 0.5 s to 1.5 s, Title moves at one speed the whole way, then shifts to another steady speed and stops dead at 3 s: that's linear, and it's why it looks mechanical. Easing makes it slow down as it leaves each keyframe and as it arrives at the next. To do it, show Title's keyframes (U), select both keys of a pair and choose **Animation > Keyframe Assistant > Easy Ease** (F9); the diamond-shaped keyframes turn into hourglasses.

Ease Title's two Position moves (0.5 s–1.5 s and 1.5 s–3 s), its Scale and its Opacity, then say done.

